1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
Do you usually go dutch when you take someone out to dinner?
你通常会在带某人出去吃饭时AA制吗？

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:07,260
Do you expect your date to pay for the whole meal?
你会期望你的约会对象支付整顿饭的费用吗？

3
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:11,880
Many people say that as long as there's love, money doesn't matter much.
许多人说，只要有爱，钱并不重要。

4
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:19,740
But this might change when the relationship gets serious and it can involve mortgages, joint current accounts and debt.
但当关系变得认真时，这种情况可能会改变，可能会涉及抵押贷款、联名活期账户和债务。

5
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:28,020
A survey in the UK suggested that 44% of married couples don't know exactly what their spouse earns.
英国的一项调查显示，44%的已婚夫妇不知道配偶的确切收入。

6
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:40,990
The research, conducted by a UK credit report service also found that an astonishing 1.9 million married couples actively try to keep their finances secret from their partners.
这项由英国信用报告服务机构进行的研究还发现，令人震惊地是居然有190万对已婚夫妇刻意试图向伴侣隐瞒财务状况。

7
00:00:40,990 --> 00:00:47,240
British relationship therapist Arabella Russell says: "It's very difficult to talk about money.
英国关系治疗师阿拉贝拉·拉塞尔（Arabella Russell）说：“讨论金钱非常困难。

8
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:49,920
Often there's guilt, there's shame.
通常会有罪恶和羞耻感。

9
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:53,210
To start those conversations is complicated.
开始这些对话很复杂。

10
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:58,320
Money can be about how we value ourselves, how we feel valued.
钱可以关乎我们如何评价自己，以及别人如何评价我们。

11
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:02,670
It's not just a simple case of talking about hard cash."
这不仅仅是谈论现金的简单问题。”

12
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:15,290
So if you are in a couple, it might be a good idea to check if you both are on the same page about money before bills pile up on the kitchen table and love flies out of the window.
所以，如果你处于恋爱关系中，在账单堆积在厨房桌上、爱情飞出窗外之前，检查一下你们是否在金钱问题上意见一致可能是个好主意。

13
00:01:15,290 --> 00:01:23,170
When moving in together, couples should not only talk about their personal habits but also about their financial ones.
当同居时，情侣们不仅应该谈论他们的个人习惯，还应该谈论他们的财务习惯。

14
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:33,840
Arabella Russell has a word of advice: "Accept the fact that in your relationship you might do money differently – there might be a spender there might be a saver.
阿拉贝拉·拉塞尔有一句忠告：“接受这样一个事实，即在你们的关系中，你们可能会以不同的方式对待金钱——可能有一个爱花钱的人，也可能有一个爱储蓄的人。

15
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:38,640
It's very tempting if your partner does things differently to say they're wrong.
如果你的伴侣做事方式与你不同，你会不自禁地想说他们是错的。

16
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:41,720
Do it differently but have a budget."
可以有不同的方式，但要有一个预算。”

17
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:44,240
And now, back to that date…
现在，回到那个约会……

18
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:50,540
Would you be put off by someone who was attractive but expected you to pay the bill by yourself?
你会被一个很有魅力但期望你自己支付账单的人吓跑吗？

19
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:52,460
There's food for thought…
这值得深思……
